     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n**Metformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day.** That is twice the FDA-labeled maximum for adults, which is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. The usual maximum single dose is about 1,000 mg. Even with normal renal function, this dose raises the risk of serious lactic acidosis.\n\nWas one of these intended?\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day and the usual maximum.\n- **1,700 mg per day total**, for example 850 mg twice daily.\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg per dose**, at a different frequency.\n\nIf you do want 1700 mg three times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note documenting that you confirmed the dose. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
